-- Passage rg8-figurative-language-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('80735e54-7cea-5d0d-b576-3115f19803a0', 'rg8-figurative-language-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-figurative-language'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Rain Check$q$, $q$The eighth-grade bake sale was supposed to start at noon on the front lawn of Westbrook Middle School. At eleven thirty, the sky opened up and rain poured down in sheets.

Tomas looked at the soggy tablecloth and the puddle forming under the cash box. "Perfect," he said. "Just the weather I ordered."

His friend Aiyana laughed and grabbed a stack of folding tables. "Come on. We can move everything into the gym lobby before the frosting melts into soup."

Inside, the lobby was crowded but dry. Tomas set out a tray of corn muffins and taped a sign above it: TRY OUR CORNY JOKES, ONE FREE WITH EVERY MUFFIN. Aiyana rolled her eyes, but she was smiling.

The first customer was Mr. Delgado, the science teacher. He leaned toward the cinnamon rolls and breathed in. "What a wonderful aroma," he said. Then he passed the garlic knots and wrinkled his nose at their strong smell, though he bought two anyway.

By two o'clock, every tray was empty. The class had raised enough money for the spring trip to the aquarium. Tomas counted the bills twice, then looked out the window at the gray sky.

"Who knew the rain would turn out to be our best salesperson?" he said. "People came inside to stay dry, and then they stayed to buy something."

Aiyana nodded. "Next year, we should order rain on purpose."$q$, 'draft')
