   $q$After finding a rule about folding lunch napkins, Faith says, "You really thought of everything." What is she actually suggesting?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rulebook is missing several important rules.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-meaning"},{"text":"She wants Kenji to add more rules about lunch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The rulebook includes far too many small, silly details.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Kenji is the smartest member of the whole club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The rulebook includes far too many small, silly details.$q$, $q$Faith uses verbal irony, and the members' snickering shows she is teasing Kenji about a rule for napkins. Taking her words as sincere praise misses the joke the others clearly understand.$q$, 'draft', '2d7f08c4-8dab-54c2-871c-7a3e1b97b79f')
