   $q$In the headline "Local Bakery Rises to the Occasion," which two meanings of "rises" does the pun use?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bread swelling as it bakes, and meeting a challenge well","is_correct":true},{"text":"A building growing taller, and bread swelling as it bakes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-context"},{"text":"Bread swelling as it bakes, and prices going up quickly","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"invented-meaning"},{"text":"Getting out of bed early, and meeting a challenge well","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-context"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Bread swelling as it bakes, and meeting a challenge well$q$, $q$The passage explains that bread rises in the oven and that rising to the occasion means meeting a challenge. Prices are never mentioned, so that choice adds a meaning the headline does not use.$q$, 'draft', 'b50ed876-622f-562a-abf8-d73bb0d6af55')
