   $q$The author says that to get a pun, "you have to notice that a word is doing double duty." What does "doing double duty" mean here?$q$, $q$[{"text":"One word is printed twice in the same headline.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"A writer has to work twice as hard on a headline.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-referent"},{"text":"One word is carrying two meanings at the same time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A reader must read every sentence two separate times.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$One word is carrying two meanings at the same time.$q$, $q$The passage defines a pun as a word with two meanings, and "double duty" means doing two jobs at once. The words are not repeated in the examples, such as "Rises" appearing only once.$q$, 'draft', 'b50ed876-622f-562a-abf8-d73bb0d6af55')
