   $q$The author ends by calling a pun "a small piece of clever craftsmanship." What does the word "craftsmanship" suggest about puns?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They are carefully built with skill and deserve respect.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They are quick jokes that take no real effort.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-connotation"},{"text":"They are printed by hand in small workshops.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They are mainly used in art classes, not reading.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-word-sense"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They are carefully built with skill and deserve respect.$q$, $q$"Craftsmanship" brings to mind a skilled maker shaping something with care, which fits the author's point that puns are worth a second look. Calling them effortless matches the "cheap tricks" view, which the ending argues against.$q$, 'draft', 'b50ed876-622f-562a-abf8-d73bb0d6af55')
