values
  ('833a619c-c322-5239-8342-6d40fd8ad1cc', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The passage ends, "Some things are worth more than the time they tell." What does this sentence suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The tower cost more money to repair than it was ever really worth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-meaning"},{"text":"The tower matters for the memories and pride it holds, not just its use.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The tower should tell stories about the town's past to visitors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-word-sense"},{"text":"The tower's clock is more accurate than any other clock in town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The tower matters for the memories and pride it holds, not just its use.$q$, $q$The sentence plays on "tell time": the tower's value goes beyond its job, as shown by people stopping to hear a sound "like an old friend." Accuracy is mentioned, but the residents' answer is about meaning, not precision.$q$, 'draft', 'fdde9a57-60d5-59d2-92d7-776db8e6d3c5')
