   $q$Why does the author open with the award instead of the first failed filter?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Knowing she succeeds, the reader focuses on how she got there.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It hides whether the filter works until the very last line.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"},{"text":"It proves the judges cared more about posters than filters.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that third place disappointed Nadia more than anything.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Knowing she succeeds, the reader focuses on how she got there.$q$, $q$Since the reader already sees the ribbon, the flashback becomes a story about the process and the failures behind the success. The outcome is revealed at the start, not hidden until the end.$q$, 'draft', '5e04c179-a9a8-5a40-9c61-0e23e6174a3f')
