   $q$Why does the author repeat the exact question "how can I build a dam quickly?" three times?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To prove that Tull forgets each answer as soon as he hears it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To set up a pattern that invites the reader to compare the answers.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To show that the animals cannot hear Tull the first time he asks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To make the fable longer without adding any new information.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-repetition-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To set up a pattern that invites the reader to compare the answers.$q$, $q$Because the question stays the same, the reader notices how each answer differs and what happens after each. Each animal answers right away, so they clearly hear him.$q$, 'draft', '2366d6b8-56e8-5831-85db-6109c8562e2c')
