-- Passage rg8-literary-structure-pov-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('cabc8f59-a363-5b75-91fe-2818cb53b2a8', 'rg8-literary-structure-pov-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Notes on the Refrigerator$q$, $q$Monday, 7:15 a.m.
Lucia, please don't use the oven after school today. I think it's making a weird noise. Better to leave it alone until after Dad's birthday. Isaac

Monday, 3:40 p.m.
Isaac, a weird noise? The oven is fine. I'm using it at 4:00 for a school project. Please stay out of the kitchen. It's a science thing. Very delicate. Lucia

Monday, 3:55 p.m.
Lucia, what science project needs an oven? Also, why is there a bag of powdered sugar hidden behind the cereal? Isaac

Monday, 4:02 p.m.
Isaac, the powdered sugar is FOR SCIENCE. Why is there a box of birthday candles in your backpack? I was only looking for a pencil. Lucia

Monday, 4:10 p.m.
Lucia, the candles are for a different science project. Please be out of the kitchen by 5:00. I need it for my experiment. Isaac

Monday, 4:12 p.m.
Isaac, your experiment wouldn't happen to be chocolate, would it? Because I already used all the chocolate. Lucia

Monday, 4:15 p.m.
Lucia, WHAT? Isaac

Monday, 6:30 p.m.
Dad, welcome home and happy birthday! Please don't open the refrigerator yet. There are two cakes in there. One is vanilla and one is chocolate (with store chocolate chips, long story). We have agreed to stop arguing until you pick a favorite. Love, Isaac and Lucia$q$, 'draft')
