-- Passage rg8-literary-structure-pov-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('8f1dbff1-9f04-534f-a72c-c1ab1455c97d', 'rg8-literary-structure-pov-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Hollis Street$q$, $q$Nothing grows on Hollis Street.
That is what the neighbors said.
The empty lot was gravel and cans,
a leaning fence, a bent bike wheel.

Then Mrs. Ito came with a shovel.
She was seventy-one years old.
She dug one square, then stopped to rest.
People watched her from their windows.

The next week, two kids from the corner
carried soil in a squeaky wagon.
A man from the laundromat brought tomato plants.
A teenager painted the fence bright blue.

By July, the lot was loud with bees.
Beans climbed the fence like ladders.
Neighbors who had never spoken
traded squash across the gate.

Now visitors stop on the sidewalk.
They ask how a garden got so green
on a block of brick and pavement.
The children hand them seed packets.
Then they tell the story from the start:
Nothing grows on Hollis Street.
That is what the neighbors said.$q$, 'draft')
