   $q$What change takes place between the first stanza and the fourth stanza?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The neighbors stop speaking to each other at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"A busy garden is paved over to make a parking lot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"},{"text":"An empty lot of gravel becomes a busy garden.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Mrs. Ito moves away and the garden is abandoned.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An empty lot of gravel becomes a busy garden.$q$, $q$The first stanza shows "gravel and cans," while the fourth shows bees, climbing beans and neighbors trading squash. The poem moves from empty to growing, not the reverse.$q$, 'draft', '8f1dbff1-9f04-534f-a72c-c1ab1455c97d')
