   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A phone receives a signal from one satellite and uses it to find its exact position. Tall buildings and indoor spaces never interfere with this process.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Satellites send timed signals that phones use to find their position. This clever system is easily the greatest invention of modern times and deserves more praise.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Phones mostly use cell towers and wireless networks to find their location. Satellites are used only as a backup when those networks are not available.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-main-and-minor"},{"text":"Satellites send timed signals, and a phone uses the delays from several of them to calculate its position. Precise clocks are essential, and other data helps when signals are blocked.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Satellites send timed signals, and a phone uses the delays from several of them to calculate its position. Precise clocks are essential, and other data helps when signals are blocked.$q$, $q$The choice about delays from several satellites covers signal timing, the need for several satellites, precise clocks and backup data without opinion. The choice saying satellites are only a backup reverses the roles, since the passage says phones add tower data "to help," not that satellites are the backup.$q$, 'draft', '961458f5-41fb-5fb6-bf4c-012a28403439')
