   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The team wins the regional contest after Mateo agrees to share his screwdriver.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"Mateo cannot fix the robot arm alone, his teammates solve the gear problem, and he shares the credit.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Mateo is a selfish student who does not deserve a place on the robotics team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Lin keeps a notebook with drawings she made in October for the robotics team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mateo cannot fix the robot arm alone, his teammates solve the gear problem, and he shares the credit.$q$, $q$An objective summary covers the main events without judgment: the failed repairs, the team's fix, and the shared credit. Calling Mateo selfish is an opinion, and the passage never says who wins the contest.$q$, 'draft', '3e8b2bb6-864c-5f74-852b-710d7e8e2ff6')
