   $q$Which sentence best states a theme of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Beavers should always build their dams downstream.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Rainstorms are dangerous for animals that live near creeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"It is wise to stay away from anyone who laughs at you.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Careful work lasts longer than work done to impress others.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Careful work lasts longer than work done to impress others.$q$, $q$Flick builds fast for an audience and his dam washes away, while Marrow's careful dam holds. Marrow does not stay away from Flick; she helps him at the end.$q$, 'draft', '36f09db0-0b06-5387-95c7-e0f4e37728ea')
