   $q$What is the theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Finishing what you start can matter more than winning.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Track races are louder and longer than people expect.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Runners should train harder so they do not finish last.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Family members should always come to watch races.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Finishing what you start can matter more than winning.$q$, $q$The speaker finishes last but says "I finished what I started. That part is mine," showing pride in finishing. The poem never suggests the speaker should have trained harder.$q$, 'draft', '101762e6-c650-57d3-aaf8-72335aace1a3')
