   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A coach teaches the whole team to count their steps during every race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-focus"},{"text":"A runner falls behind, thinks about quitting, keeps going, and finishes last with pride.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A runner quits halfway through the race but is cheered on by her sister.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"A brave runner gives an inspiring effort that every reader should admire.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A runner falls behind, thinks about quitting, keeps going, and finishes last with pride.$q$, $q$This choice tracks the main events of the race without judging them. "Brave" and "inspiring" are opinions, and the speaker does not quit but crosses the line.$q$, 'draft', '101762e6-c650-57d3-aaf8-72335aace1a3')
