   $q$How does the second stanza contribute to the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the speaker has already decided to stop running.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It states the theme that no one keeps track of slower runners.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail-with-theme"},{"text":"It shows the speaker's temptation to quit, which makes the choice to continue meaningful.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It describes the weather in order to create a calm mood.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows the speaker's temptation to quit, which makes the choice to continue meaningful.$q$, $q$The voice saying "I could stop" creates a real choice, so continuing shows the theme. The line that no one keeps a list is part of the temptation, not the poem's lesson.$q$, 'draft', '101762e6-c650-57d3-aaf8-72335aace1a3')
