  ('71126155-a8ac-5ef2-ad7a-22255bbf6d02', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix inter- means "between," and the root rupt means "break." What does "interrupted" mean in the sentence about the clouds?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ended the viewing for the rest of the night","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Broke into the viewing and stopped it for a while","is_correct":true},{"text":"Moved slowly between the stars without effect","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Made the view of the planets much clearer","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Broke into the viewing and stopped it for a while$q$, $q$Inter plus rupt means "break between," so the clouds broke into the viewing, and the passage says the pause lasted twenty minutes before the clouds cleared. The viewing did not end for the night, so the choice "Ended the viewing for the rest of the night" goes too far.$q$, 'draft', 'a4792192-98aa-5cd4-acce-a891dbc9edfb')
