   $q$What is the author's main claim about the end of Halvering's ice trade?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The paper mill closed the ice company on purpose in 1905.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Several problems weakened the trade before refrigerators finished it off.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Electric refrigerators were the only reason the ice trade ended.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The ice trade ended because workers no longer wanted to cut ice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Several problems weakened the trade before refrigerators finished it off.$q$, $q$The author says the refrigerator was "the final blow to an industry that was already failing" and points to pollution, weather and factories. The passage argues against the idea that refrigerators alone were to blame.$q$, 'draft', 'd76e6eab-a516-5fac-a383-59c5b56b08a6')
