   $q$How does the author respond to the argument that one small tower cannot do any harm?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author agrees fully and decides that small towers are acceptable.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The author rejects the point by saying even one stone kills every insect.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"The author grants the point for one tower but shows that many visitors add up.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author ignores the point and moves on to a different topic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overlooks-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author grants the point for one tower but shows that many visitors add up.$q$, $q$The author writes "That may be true of a single tower" and then uses the forty thousand yearly visitors to show the combined effect. The author never claims one stone kills every insect.$q$, 'draft', 'b216a66a-35df-58fb-bf9d-6c70662ac876')
