  ('dd77c130-f6b0-5807-b6bb-d9c7c7930a63', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-argument-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence from the passage contains faulty reasoning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The stones in a creek are not just decoration.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-fallacy"},{"text":"Besides, everyone I know thinks rock towers look silly, so clearly most people already agree with me.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In some parks, rangers build small rock piles to mark trails where the path is hard to see.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-fallacy"},{"text":"Connection to nature is valuable, but there are ways to enjoy the creek that do not change it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-fallacy"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Besides, everyone I know thinks rock towers look silly, so clearly most people already agree with me.$q$, $q$The author's own friends are a small, unrepresentative group, and what people find silly does not show whether stacking harms the creek. The sentence about ranger piles is a fact that explains why stacks can confuse hikers.$q$, 'draft', 'b216a66a-35df-58fb-bf9d-6c70662ac876')
