   $q$What is the author's main purpose in this essay?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To tell a funny story about the author's nephew visiting the farm","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To argue that grocery stores should stop selling fresh vegetables","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"To persuade shoppers to buy oddly shaped produce instead of passing it by","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain how farmers grow carrots in different kinds of soil","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To persuade shoppers to buy oddly shaped produce instead of passing it by$q$, $q$The essay ends with direct requests: "look for the strange ones" and "Buy the pepper with the dent." The nephew and Gerald only introduce that argument, so the story choice is too narrow.$q$, 'draft', '35cd9fa5-dae1-53c2-8ac2-408db2fc21f0')
