   $q$Which statement best describes the author's point of view about drawing in a museum?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Drawing is a pleasant break for students who are bored by paintings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"Drawing matters less than learning the history of each painting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"},{"text":"Drawing helps young people look at art more closely and carefully.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Drawing should be allowed only for students who plan to become artists.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Drawing helps young people look at art more closely and carefully.$q$, $q$The author writes "Drawing is not a distraction from looking," and calls it "the best way to look closely." That directly rejects the idea that drawing is a break from the art.$q$, 'draft', 'f24dc6a5-9f39-514d-9926-0117136c9ec1')
